      ],
      "impact": "The EPD panel's internal booster control loop reads the source current through R1; a 1000× error makes the current-sense feedback meaningless, so the boost converter will not regulate the high voltage correctly (the e-paper panel will fail to refresh, and the loop may over-current the MOSFET/diodes).",
      "confidence": 0.6
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet the input/decoupling capacitor C1 on the Display_Power_Switch rail is drawn as '0.1uF/16V'.",
      "expected": "The specification's component table assigns C1 the PDI default value of 1 µF / 25 V (C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C1 / 0.1uF/16V (EPD_Driver.kicad_sch, Display_Power_Switch to GND)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"}
      ],
      "impact": "Ten times less bulk capacitance on the EPD power rail feeding the boost converter increases input ripple and can destabilize the booster under load, deviating from the intended PDI reference behaviour.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The two hierarchical sub-sheets otherwise match the specification, but on the EPD_Driver sheet two passive values deviate from the intended design: the booster current-sense resistor R1 is shown as 0.47 kΩ instead of the specified 0.47 Ω (a three-order-of-magnitude error that breaks the boost current feedback), and the rail decoupling capacitor C1 is shown as 0.1 µF/16 V instead of the specified 1 µF/25 V."
}

